        "heading": "TOP SECRET SCIENCE (For Big and Small Brains)",
        "body_label": "Scientific Fact:",
        "body": "The brain uses a lot of energy to switch tasks (from resting to working). This is called Limbic Friction. By proposing 'only 10 minutes', Mimi lowered the friction. It's like lowering the height of a hurdle so Dilo could jump over it easily. Once he was running, his brain released adrenaline and dopamine, making it easy to keep going!"
